    "updated_at": "2026-10-05T13:34:04Z",
    "body": "@DavidBuchanan314 DavidBuchanan314 Fair question \u2014 I should have pointed to the concrete result instead of linking the whole research log.\r\n\r\nThe analysis was carried out by AIODAM, an autonomous research agent I built, rather than by me manually. I provided my camera for the device-side observation and published the work.\r\n\r\nOne concrete finding was an unencrypted SSH private key inside the decrypted A7S III firmware. The host key observed on my camera did not match it, so this is not evidence of working authentication or an exploit.\r\n\r\nYour decryption work made the analysis possible. Neither the firmware-decryption key nor the first confirmation of A7S III compatibility is our discovery.\r\n\r\nHere is the [[short findings summary](https://github.com/oxunjonuz/aiodam-sony-a7siii-firmware-audit#scope-and-findings)](https://github.com/oxunjonuz/aiodam-sony-a7siii-firmware-audit#scope-and-findings). Do you recognize that embedded SSH key as a known development/test artifact?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
